    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0342" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-18T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 3:11 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>118. Department’s unnumbered instructions July 18.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d152-f1"
                    /> Foreign Office advises Italian Government will be glad to furnish American
                    officer with all information and data he may require for fulfillment of mission
                    in connection with preparations for round-the-world flight of Army
                    aeroplanes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
